        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'This is an evolving area of UAE law. Federal Decree-Law No. 26 of 2025 on Child Digital Safety (in force January 2026) requires that parents or guardians refrain from displaying or negatively exploiting a child online in a way that threatens the child\'s privacy, dignity, or wellbeing. In practice, Abu Dhabi courts have treated posting children\'s images online as a decision requiring joint parental consent, in the same category as travel and educational decisions. If your ex-partner objects to you posting images of your children, they can apply to court for an order restricting this.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
