      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'Either parent can apply to the Personal Status Court (or the Abu Dhabi Civil Family Court if applicable) for an urgent travel restriction order. You will need to show that there is a genuine risk the child will be removed from the UAE. The court can issue the order on an urgent basis and it is enforced at all UAE airports and land borders through the immigration system. The child\'s passport is typically held by the guardian (father) under UAE law, but courts can order it transferred to the mother.',
      },
