        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'UAE does not recognise dual nationality for UAE citizens. If your child holds UAE nationality (typically through the father), UAE law requires them to enter and exit the UAE on their UAE passport. The UAE passport is what UAE border authorities use to flag the child under a travel ban. However, once the child reaches the UK on their British passport, UK authorities recognise them as a British citizen. This means a UAE custody order is not automatically enforceable in the UK. You would need to register or mirror the UAE order in a UK family court.',
      },
    },
